three.ws Forge is a fork of Modly, a desktop application for local image-to-3D
generation. Modly is released under the MIT License; its full text, including
the attribution request quoted above, is in the LICENSE file in this
directory and applies to the code that originates from Modly. The three.ws
changes (the rebrand, the three.ws account and publishing integration, the
three.ws Forge cloud generators bundled from integrations/modly, the CC0
library browser, and the release pipeline) are released under the same MIT
License.

Model extensions that Forge installs from GitHub (for example the Hunyuan3D,
TRELLIS and TripoSG extensions published by Lightning Pixel) download model
weights from their original publishers. Those weights carry their own
licenses, which Forge shows on each model's card before download. Tencent's
Hunyuan3D weights in particular are licensed for use outside the European
Union, the United Kingdom and South Korea only.
